# where a locally-run process keeps its pidfile and log
.run/

# Compiled binaries.
#
# `go build ./services/...` from the workspace root writes each command's
# binary into the directory it was run from, or into the service directory,
# and a twenty megabyte file is easy to commit without noticing. Named by the
# convention every command here follows, so a new service is covered the day
# it is written: <name>d for a daemon, plus the two that predate it.
/core
/*d
services/*/core
services/*/dashboard
services/*/*d
# frontend
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
